# Headers for the files Cloudflare serves without waking the Worker. Parsed at
# deploy time, never served; paths are the ones in the client build output.
#
# Cloudflare's default for a static asset is `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which
# is the safe choice for a name that can change meaning. It is the wrong one for
# a build asset: the name already contains a hash of the contents, so a changed
# file is a changed URL, and every revalidation of the old one is a round trip
# that can only ever answer 304.
#
# Nothing else is listed on purpose. An icon, the manifest and `sw.js` all keep
# their names across a deploy, and `sw.js` in particular is how a stale app
# learns there is a new one — a service worker nobody revalidates is a version
# of the site that never ends.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
